WEBVTT

00:00:05.820 --> 00:00:07.770
He cleared his psychological evaluation.

00:00:08.450 --> 00:00:11.610
No signs of abnormality or 
violence during observation,

00:00:12.180 --> 00:00:15.140
but reports do indicate an inability 
to adapt to society.

00:00:15.140 --> 00:00:16.830
Of course...

00:00:16.830 --> 00:00:19.620
Since he was a kid, he hasn't
been part of normal society.

00:00:21.080 --> 00:00:23.580
Many committee members agree.

00:00:24.150 --> 00:00:25.920
As opposed to Hachijou, AKA Bird,

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:28.540
they say he wants to be part of the community.

00:00:28.790 --> 00:00:30.670
So the permission we were given...

00:00:31.020 --> 00:00:33.340
Feel free to think of it as a test.

00:00:33.750 --> 00:00:37.070
Whether Japan accepts him or erases him...

00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:40.930
Well, that will be his choice.

00:00:49.700 --> 00:00:50.910
Sis...

00:00:50.910 --> 00:00:53.000
Don't worry. This place is safe.

00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:54.490
I've been here several times.

00:00:54.770 --> 00:00:55.990
He's an interesting guy.

00:00:57.120 --> 00:00:58.410
See, we're here.

00:00:58.410 --> 00:00:59.450
R-Right.

00:01:03.660 --> 00:01:06.190
The seething sea ceaseth, 
thus the seething sea sufficeth us.

00:01:07.210 --> 00:01:09.840
<i>Voice pattern and password match.</i>

00:01:09.840 --> 00:01:11.410
<i>Please come in.</i>

00:01:11.410 --> 00:01:12.430
Thanks.

00:01:16.380 --> 00:01:19.250
Hey! How are you doing?

00:01:20.010 --> 00:01:22.730
I brought you some stuff, young man!

00:01:31.710 --> 00:01:32.900
<i>In the future,</i>

00:01:32.900 --> 00:01:36.350
<i>when something happens beyond 
the normal police's capacity,</i>

00:01:36.350 --> 00:01:39.370
<i>they turn to the power of the ACTIVE project.</i>

00:01:40.760 --> 00:01:45.700
<i>This is the story of Japan's ACTIVE, 
the Third Mobile Assault Unit.</i>

00:02:59.820 --> 00:03:03.030
<b>File 4: Mythos, Once More</b>

00:03:04.170 --> 00:03:05.340
What is it now?

00:03:06.160 --> 00:03:08.040
None of this is even remotely entertaining.

00:03:08.040 --> 00:03:09.790
Oh, don't be like that!

00:03:10.050 --> 00:03:11.540
This time, I brought Chinchirorin.

00:03:12.470 --> 00:03:13.540
I'm sure today, you still—

00:03:13.540 --> 00:03:16.230
Well, if you won't play with me,

00:03:16.230 --> 00:03:17.760
I'll just hang out here forever.

00:03:18.790 --> 00:03:20.570
Then, I'll start by explaining the rules.

00:03:19.190 --> 00:03:20.110
Well?

00:03:20.570 --> 00:03:23.380
Supposedly, he was the boy 
partnered with Hachijou Tomoki.

00:03:24.940 --> 00:03:26.620
I don't know how to say it,

00:03:26.930 --> 00:03:30.460
but he's totally different from Hachijou-senpai.

00:03:30.980 --> 00:03:31.750
I see.

00:03:33.100 --> 00:03:35.360
That's thirty-two straight wins for me.

00:03:36.330 --> 00:03:39.110
It appears even Lady Luck has abandoned you.

00:03:39.440 --> 00:03:42.980
Why is Kuroki-san playing games with him?

00:03:39.440 --> 00:03:42.980
Damn it! I was sure I could win with this!

00:03:42.980 --> 00:03:44.840
One more time.

00:03:42.980 --> 00:03:47.470
To insure against recidivism, 
it's best that society accepts him.

00:03:47.470 --> 00:03:50.410
Kuroki-kun says for that to work,

00:03:50.410 --> 00:03:52.460
Mythos needs to make friends with someone.

00:03:52.460 --> 00:03:53.690
Huh?

00:03:53.860 --> 00:03:56.780
He looks a little scary, but he's nice, isn't he?

00:03:56.780 --> 00:03:57.420
Yeah.

00:03:59.090 --> 00:04:00.010
What?

00:04:00.010 --> 00:04:01.480
I saw this back there, too,

00:04:01.480 --> 00:04:04.090
but you really have your act together
when you're working, huh?

00:04:04.960 --> 00:04:07.510
Why are you such a failure 
at life when you're at home?

00:04:08.070 --> 00:04:10.390
Am I that much of a failure?

00:04:10.640 --> 00:04:11.860
Yes, you are.

00:04:11.860 --> 00:04:13.220
How am I a failure?

00:04:13.220 --> 00:04:14.380
Tell me!

00:04:14.380 --> 00:04:17.000
Well, for one, you failed to 
notice that you're a failure!

00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:17.730
I failed?

00:04:18.990 --> 00:04:20.440
Hey, young man...

00:04:21.060 --> 00:04:22.650
Interested in the outside?

00:04:24.230 --> 00:04:25.220
It doesn't matter.

00:04:25.520 --> 00:04:27.530
Liko's back to normal.

00:04:27.900 --> 00:04:30.470
The chaos you caused is over.

00:04:31.800 --> 00:04:35.000
Hachijou escaped overseas
using extralegal measures—

00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:36.100
I don't care!

00:04:45.010 --> 00:04:46.440
That bastard...

00:04:56.370 --> 00:04:57.130
Unmanned—

00:04:57.130 --> 00:04:58.200
You're so slow!

00:04:58.200 --> 00:04:59.940
Get a move on!

00:04:59.940 --> 00:05:02.530
Um, this is to apologize for yesterday.

00:04:59.940 --> 00:05:05.450
<b>The Records of Doryuugou</b>

00:05:02.530 --> 00:05:05.450
No, that was needed to solve the case.

00:05:05.450 --> 00:05:08.170
No, not only did I use your 
singing without permission,

00:05:08.170 --> 00:05:10.550
I made you clean up after the party!

00:05:10.550 --> 00:05:11.620
I have to give you something...

00:05:11.620 --> 00:05:15.330
It's partially my responsibility for calling Unit 9.

00:05:15.330 --> 00:05:18.020
But I still wouldn't feel right!

00:05:18.020 --> 00:05:19.470
Sorry, Asami-chan!

00:05:19.470 --> 00:05:21.300
We have to get going.

00:05:21.300 --> 00:05:23.260
Oh... Yes, great.

00:05:23.540 --> 00:05:25.180
So we're off to Davos

00:05:25.180 --> 00:05:28.340
for the International 
Anti-Terrorism Conference.

00:05:28.340 --> 00:05:31.100
Kuroki-kun will be placed

00:05:31.100 --> 00:05:32.470
in charge of Unit 3.

00:05:32.470 --> 00:05:33.910
Understood!

00:05:33.910 --> 00:05:35.880
Take care of West Japan, too.

00:05:35.880 --> 00:05:38.080
Yeah, leave it to me!

00:05:38.080 --> 00:05:39.380
Great...

00:05:40.930 --> 00:05:42.600
U-Um, boss...

00:05:42.600 --> 00:05:45.750
I put all the reference materials 
you'll need in this.

00:05:46.320 --> 00:05:47.940
Please take it!

00:05:47.940 --> 00:05:49.380
Th-Thank you.

00:05:49.380 --> 00:05:50.700
Take care.

00:05:51.450 --> 00:05:54.500
Acting chief? You?

00:05:54.500 --> 00:05:55.260
Yeah.

00:05:54.500 --> 00:05:58.960
<b>Unit 8</b>

00:05:55.260 --> 00:05:58.970
So if something happens, 
you have to obey my orders... uh...

00:06:00.330 --> 00:06:02.520
Why do you look so dissatisfied?

00:06:02.840 --> 00:06:06.800
Well, my company will simply 
act according to its contract.

00:06:08.090 --> 00:06:11.000
So this is the chief's chair?

00:06:11.000 --> 00:06:12.660
Actually, it's not that different.

00:06:12.660 --> 00:06:14.310
They're government-issued, after all.

00:06:14.310 --> 00:06:16.600
Um, someone from the media

00:06:16.600 --> 00:06:18.980
wants to talk to the acting chief.

00:06:18.980 --> 00:06:19.940
Fine!

00:06:21.260 --> 00:06:22.210
All yours.

00:06:23.730 --> 00:06:24.930
All mine?

00:06:28.410 --> 00:06:30.410
Komi-Eri-chan! Hey there!

00:06:30.410 --> 00:06:32.030
Oh? Kuroki-san?

00:06:32.030 --> 00:06:34.150
I'm the acting chief right now.

00:06:34.150 --> 00:06:35.260
I see.

00:06:35.760 --> 00:06:37.000
That might be better.

00:06:37.770 --> 00:06:40.300
I wanted to ask you something off the record.

00:06:40.620 --> 00:06:43.770
About that incident that took 
down all the city systems,

00:06:43.770 --> 00:06:45.560
the Logos Incident...

00:06:46.020 --> 00:06:49.340
There's a rumor that an 
underage boy was involved.

00:06:49.340 --> 00:06:50.830
There is, huh?

00:06:51.190 --> 00:06:54.810
It's hard to imagine a minor 
causing all that chaos, but...

00:06:55.430 --> 00:06:57.470
Well, if there's one thing I can say,

00:06:57.470 --> 00:06:59.770
it's that you can still start over at that age.

00:07:00.300 --> 00:07:01.270
That's off the record, okay?

00:07:01.520 --> 00:07:04.700
While we're off the record,
let me ask about Governor Inagi!

00:07:04.700 --> 00:07:06.450
That's what you're really after, huh?

00:07:07.310 --> 00:07:09.540
I'm counting on you, Acting Chief!

00:07:10.250 --> 00:07:11.450
Good work today!

00:07:11.450 --> 00:07:13.370
Okay, a toast to the acting chief!

00:07:13.370 --> 00:07:14.410
Cheers!

00:07:19.130 --> 00:07:23.080
You sure this is a good idea, 
when we're already short-staffed?

00:07:31.260 --> 00:07:32.550
Reporting in.

00:07:32.550 --> 00:07:34.710
Highway 6, point B, nothing.

00:07:35.010 --> 00:07:36.970
Located a vehicle believed to be the target.

00:07:36.970 --> 00:07:37.980
In pursuit.

00:07:37.980 --> 00:07:39.020
Don't underestimate us!

00:07:43.280 --> 00:07:44.330
Target sighted.

00:07:44.900 --> 00:07:46.150
No one's riding it!

00:07:46.150 --> 00:07:48.730
So it matches the report. An unmanned, 
remote-control vehicle?

00:07:49.820 --> 00:07:51.640
Oh, no! A pedestrian!

00:07:55.570 --> 00:07:57.780
You lost the target?!

00:07:58.830 --> 00:08:01.680
I guess we should contact Unit 8...

00:08:05.700 --> 00:08:06.380
Hey.

00:08:06.380 --> 00:08:07.800
What is it now?

00:08:07.800 --> 00:08:09.750
Something I wanted to ask you.

00:08:10.040 --> 00:08:12.340
The Willwear you used before...

00:08:12.340 --> 00:08:14.150
Did you have a second one ready?

00:08:14.710 --> 00:08:16.060
Free Delta?

00:08:16.590 --> 00:08:17.260
No.

00:08:17.260 --> 00:08:19.720
You didn't give it to someone else again, right?

00:08:20.610 --> 00:08:22.420
Giving the orders from here?

00:08:22.420 --> 00:08:25.580
Is security that weak at this prison?

00:08:25.580 --> 00:08:27.180
This safe house!

00:08:27.640 --> 00:08:31.770
So someone, somewhere, is using 
the same type of Willwear

00:08:31.770 --> 00:08:33.900
to cause some kind of trouble.

00:08:34.180 --> 00:08:35.560
Correct?

00:08:37.810 --> 00:08:38.590
Well?

00:08:39.210 --> 00:08:41.000
That certainly is Free Delta.

00:08:41.670 --> 00:08:44.160
But it doesn't seem to have 
been customized like mine.

00:08:44.480 --> 00:08:46.640
Who do you think it is, and what's their plan?

00:08:46.640 --> 00:08:49.380
Why do I have to answer that?

00:08:50.460 --> 00:08:51.560
That's true.

00:08:51.890 --> 00:08:53.690
Bye, then. I'll be back.

00:08:58.260 --> 00:08:59.330
The light!

00:08:59.330 --> 00:09:00.220
Brake!

00:09:04.560 --> 00:09:05.480
Damn it!

00:09:05.760 --> 00:09:07.150
This is Car 4.

00:09:06.210 --> 00:09:09.960
Why do the lights always change 
right when it needs them to?

00:09:07.150 --> 00:09:10.440
Target lost near East Elementary School.
Requesting immediate backup.

00:09:11.200 --> 00:09:13.400
<i>A mysterious motorcycle is 
rampaging through the city.</i>

00:09:13.690 --> 00:09:17.360
<i>It's shaken off pursuit by the police's 
Mobile Traffic Unit multiple times.</i>

00:09:17.630 --> 00:09:19.250
<i>What is its goal?</i>

00:09:19.550 --> 00:09:22.040
<i>Will it be out again tonight?</i>

00:09:22.370 --> 00:09:24.460
<i>This concludes my report from the scene.</i>

00:09:25.000 --> 00:09:28.630
I can't believe we can't go out there.

00:09:28.630 --> 00:09:32.050
The guys in Traffic Investigation 
have a lot of pride...

00:09:32.050 --> 00:09:35.190
Is that why they haven't asked us for support,

00:09:35.190 --> 00:09:36.860
even though it's a Willwear incident?

00:09:36.860 --> 00:09:38.050
However,

00:09:38.050 --> 00:09:41.000
it's not much of an incident.

00:09:41.000 --> 00:09:43.770
Yeah, only traffic violations.

00:09:44.470 --> 00:09:45.980
Come to think of it,

00:09:45.980 --> 00:09:48.480
the guys in Mobile Traffic 
said something strange.

00:09:48.790 --> 00:09:52.690
Traffic lights turn green
everywhere the motorcycle goes.

00:09:52.690 --> 00:09:54.720
Does that mean someone's

00:09:54.720 --> 00:09:57.140
hacking the system and controlling the lights?

00:09:57.140 --> 00:09:58.660
No, actually,

00:09:58.930 --> 00:10:02.120
the Traffic Control Center 
says that's not happening.

00:10:02.510 --> 00:10:05.130
There's no sign of a hack,

00:10:05.130 --> 00:10:08.330
and the lights are under control.

00:10:08.330 --> 00:10:09.540
That leaves...

00:10:09.900 --> 00:10:12.800
Controlling the lights directly, at the scene?

00:10:12.800 --> 00:10:14.450
All right, Head Patrol Officer Kaburagi!

00:10:14.450 --> 00:10:15.310
Y-Yes, sir!

00:10:15.610 --> 00:10:17.380
You're going to question people at the scene.

00:10:17.380 --> 00:10:20.370
What?! At the scene? I... I...

00:10:20.370 --> 00:10:22.390
I grant permission to use your glasses.

00:10:26.120 --> 00:10:27.720
How's it been lately?

00:10:27.720 --> 00:10:29.280
Okay, I guess...

00:10:29.650 --> 00:10:31.250
May I ask you something?

00:10:32.530 --> 00:10:35.320
I guess she can do it, after all.

00:10:36.060 --> 00:10:37.200
Excuse me!

00:10:37.200 --> 00:10:37.900
Huh?!

00:10:38.140 --> 00:10:39.720
Um, have you...

00:10:38.460 --> 00:10:39.720
Hey, you alone?

00:10:39.720 --> 00:10:41.490
I know a place you can make good money.

00:10:41.810 --> 00:10:43.710
Have you heard of the "ghost bike"?

00:10:42.240 --> 00:10:43.710
You with a magazine or TV?

00:10:43.710 --> 00:10:45.060
That's hilarious!

00:10:47.030 --> 00:10:49.580
I asked all around the city, and no one saw

00:10:49.580 --> 00:10:51.470
anyone suspicious near the light

00:10:51.470 --> 00:10:55.000
control panels during the incidents 
with the motorcycle Willwear.

00:10:55.000 --> 00:10:56.260
Good work.

00:10:56.260 --> 00:10:58.720
I'm amazed you were able to get 
that much witness testimony!

00:10:58.720 --> 00:11:01.180
Yes, many people who are making

00:11:01.180 --> 00:11:04.340
prolonged pit stops in the 
race of life helped me.

00:11:04.340 --> 00:11:06.950
If the press heard you say that, 
there'd be an uproar!

00:11:07.270 --> 00:11:08.930
I'm taking these back.

00:11:08.930 --> 00:11:10.930
No! Please, no...

00:11:09.690 --> 00:11:10.930
Sorry.

00:11:10.930 --> 00:11:12.860
Acting chief's orders.

00:11:12.860 --> 00:11:13.860
That's right!

00:11:13.860 --> 00:11:15.860
You don't need to rely on those...

00:11:15.860 --> 00:11:17.690
Er, what's this?

00:11:17.690 --> 00:11:20.820
Witness reports I had an
acquaintance collect for me.

00:11:21.190 --> 00:11:22.630
About that Willwear.

00:11:22.630 --> 00:11:23.780
Thanks.

00:11:25.990 --> 00:11:28.120
So that motorcycle Willwear...

00:11:28.370 --> 00:11:32.370
Everywhere it goes, the lights turn green.

00:11:32.760 --> 00:11:34.880
The Traffic Control Center 
says nothing's wrong.

00:11:35.120 --> 00:11:37.880
And there's no sign of the lights 
being altered directly.

00:11:38.140 --> 00:11:39.160
So how?

00:11:42.260 --> 00:11:43.870
The control center

00:11:44.170 --> 00:11:47.530
uses road data on traffic levels

00:11:47.530 --> 00:11:50.860
in order to adjust the lights 
and avoid congestion.

00:11:51.510 --> 00:11:55.620
If someone rewrote that traffic flow data...

00:11:56.210 --> 00:11:57.150
What would happen?

00:11:58.110 --> 00:11:59.240
Shall I show you?

00:11:59.240 --> 00:12:01.150
Can you do that?

00:12:01.150 --> 00:12:02.030
Hey!

00:12:01.410 --> 00:12:02.820
Nope...

00:12:02.820 --> 00:12:05.740
I'm not letting you on the Internet yet!

00:12:12.280 --> 00:12:14.120
Hey, it's morning.

00:12:16.770 --> 00:12:18.030
You stayed all night?

00:12:18.750 --> 00:12:22.340
I was running all over until after the last train.

00:12:22.880 --> 00:12:23.990
Morning.

00:12:23.990 --> 00:12:25.540
Good morning.

00:12:25.540 --> 00:12:26.850
So how's it going?

00:12:26.850 --> 00:12:32.310
Traffic Investigation says this case 
is theirs, and they don't need us.

00:12:32.310 --> 00:12:35.240
Then, why not claim we're investigating

00:12:35.240 --> 00:12:36.910
the traffic flow monitors?

00:12:36.910 --> 00:12:38.140
I see...

00:12:38.440 --> 00:12:39.370
All right!

00:12:39.370 --> 00:12:42.650
Third Mobile Assault Unit 8, roll out!

00:12:42.650 --> 00:12:45.110
You just wanted to say that, didn't you?

00:12:53.840 --> 00:12:57.920
If we're investigating traffic flow monitors, 
why are we taking this?

00:12:59.670 --> 00:13:03.510
The acting chief just wanted to do it, probably.

00:13:03.840 --> 00:13:06.610
Kuroki-san, the ghost bike has appeared.

00:13:08.300 --> 00:13:10.850
This is where good luck comes in handy!

00:13:11.500 --> 00:13:13.370
This is Mobile Unit 105.

00:13:13.370 --> 00:13:15.370
Heading south on Highway 16.

00:13:15.370 --> 00:13:16.060
I repeat...

00:13:18.010 --> 00:13:19.160
You were right!

00:13:19.160 --> 00:13:21.770
The data doesn't match the real traffic flow!

00:13:21.770 --> 00:13:24.030
Okay, I'll go and solve the case.

00:13:24.270 --> 00:13:26.300
No. You don't have permission.

00:13:26.300 --> 00:13:27.990
That doesn't matter. We can get it later.

00:13:27.990 --> 00:13:29.060
It does matter.

00:13:29.060 --> 00:13:30.660
If there's a problem, I'll be—

00:13:30.660 --> 00:13:34.040
Ever since you went civilian, 
you've turned boring.

00:13:34.040 --> 00:13:34.940
What did you say?

00:13:34.940 --> 00:13:36.660
Public servants are those 
with steady paychecks—

00:13:36.660 --> 00:13:39.470
You're the one who threw that 
steady paycheck away!

00:13:40.390 --> 00:13:42.510
This is a good time for me to ask...

00:13:42.510 --> 00:13:44.550
Why did you quit the police?

00:13:44.550 --> 00:13:46.180
You were on the fast track to promotion.

00:13:46.180 --> 00:13:47.600
I told you.

00:13:47.600 --> 00:13:50.710
To take responsibility for launching without 
permission during the Logos Incident—

00:13:50.710 --> 00:13:53.410
The police chief said there was no need for that!

00:13:53.410 --> 00:13:53.970
That's...

00:13:53.970 --> 00:13:56.100
You're too weak, mentally.

00:13:56.100 --> 00:13:57.690
Whenever things get bad, you run.

00:13:58.040 --> 00:13:59.080
I bet I know what it was.

00:13:59.080 --> 00:14:01.570
You wanted to get away from 
Lieutenant Ooshikouchi!

00:14:01.570 --> 00:14:03.460
You ass!

00:14:03.460 --> 00:14:05.480
You quit the fast track with 
the Ministry of Defense.

00:14:05.480 --> 00:14:07.300
You quit the fast track with the cops.

00:14:07.300 --> 00:14:09.110
What are you trying to accomplish?!

00:14:09.110 --> 00:14:10.590
It's none of your business!

00:14:10.590 --> 00:14:14.370
Then why are you so relaxed 
about promotions?!

00:14:14.370 --> 00:14:15.650
What do you mean, relaxed?!

00:14:14.990 --> 00:14:16.950
Stop it, you two.

00:14:15.650 --> 00:14:18.070
That's what I hate about you!

00:14:16.950 --> 00:14:18.070
Hey!

00:14:18.670 --> 00:14:21.170
The unmanned Willwear has disappeared.

00:14:22.210 --> 00:14:22.990
Right.

00:14:25.090 --> 00:14:25.760
Hey.

00:14:25.760 --> 00:14:27.050
Well?

00:14:27.290 --> 00:14:29.080
You were right.

00:14:29.380 --> 00:14:31.710
The traffic flow data was altered.

00:14:32.070 --> 00:14:33.010
I see.

00:14:33.010 --> 00:14:36.040
But what's that Willwear trying to do?

00:14:36.040 --> 00:14:38.050
It's popping up all over the city,

00:14:38.050 --> 00:14:40.440
as if it just wants to screw with us.

00:14:40.850 --> 00:14:43.400
It races along for a while and disappears.

00:14:43.870 --> 00:14:46.410
Its appearances are so random, 
we can't use checkpoints.

00:14:46.760 --> 00:14:49.330
If only we could guess where 
it will appear next...

00:14:49.610 --> 00:14:50.800
What about the transit routes?

00:14:52.030 --> 00:14:54.370
Trace the routes it's traveled.

00:14:58.710 --> 00:14:59.830
How's it going?

00:14:59.830 --> 00:15:03.670
We traced the transit routes the target used,

00:15:03.670 --> 00:15:06.630
then eliminated everything but 
those it used multiple times.

00:15:06.630 --> 00:15:07.740
This is what's left.

00:15:12.360 --> 00:15:13.460
"Rider"?

00:15:13.460 --> 00:15:15.110
Because it's a bike?

00:15:15.110 --> 00:15:17.370
It's screwing with us!

00:15:17.670 --> 00:15:20.060
Doesn't that mean it's over?

00:15:20.060 --> 00:15:22.650
I guess next could be an "S," for "Riders."

00:15:22.900 --> 00:15:24.850
Or since it's unmanned,

00:15:24.850 --> 00:15:27.480
next could be the "L" in "Riderless."

00:15:27.480 --> 00:15:30.370
Like, it could head east at the 
bottom right of the screen?

00:15:30.370 --> 00:15:32.360
Shall we tell police HQ?

00:15:33.530 --> 00:15:37.210
We can tell them about "Rider" 
and the green traffic lights.

00:15:37.210 --> 00:15:39.540
For everything else, we have more work to do.

00:15:39.540 --> 00:15:42.170
Right. We can tell them when we're certain.

00:15:42.430 --> 00:15:43.790
Okay, take care of contacting them.

00:15:44.060 --> 00:15:45.140
Where are you going?

00:15:45.140 --> 00:15:46.670
I'm off to hear the rest.

00:15:46.670 --> 00:15:47.700
To hear it?

00:15:47.700 --> 00:15:48.630
From whom?

00:15:48.630 --> 00:15:49.490
No idea.

00:15:50.620 --> 00:15:52.330
You were right.

00:15:52.330 --> 00:15:56.100
We traced the transit route, 
and the word "Rider" appeared.

00:15:56.100 --> 00:15:57.050
Yeah?

00:15:57.050 --> 00:15:59.440
I wonder where he'll show up next...

00:15:59.440 --> 00:16:01.580
I wonder what letter it will be!

00:16:02.900 --> 00:16:06.110
Do you get some benefit in 
not telling me everything?

00:16:06.110 --> 00:16:08.240
I dislike doing things this way.

00:16:08.240 --> 00:16:10.450
Tell me all your information on them.

00:16:10.820 --> 00:16:11.990
You're right.

00:16:14.820 --> 00:16:18.810
If the "them" you're referring to 
is Hachijou... no, Bird,

00:16:19.300 --> 00:16:21.540
there's more to this than it looks like.

00:16:22.140 --> 00:16:24.860
She went to school with Bird's public identity,

00:16:24.860 --> 00:16:27.250
high school student Hachijou Tomoki.

00:16:28.040 --> 00:16:29.160
Don't worry.

00:16:29.160 --> 00:16:31.350
He won't bite.

00:16:31.720 --> 00:16:34.110
Um, nice to meet you.

00:16:34.690 --> 00:16:36.990
No, this isn't our first meeting.

00:16:38.020 --> 00:16:40.470
I was looking into Bird, and I found you.

00:16:41.470 --> 00:16:45.350
What was the Hachijou-senpai you knew like?

00:16:46.450 --> 00:16:48.320
Here are our investigation files.

00:16:48.620 --> 00:16:50.070
Go over them together.

00:16:50.070 --> 00:16:51.130
Is it all right?

00:16:51.130 --> 00:16:52.850
We're still watching you, just in case.

00:16:53.170 --> 00:16:54.910
He didn't have to tell him.

00:16:55.300 --> 00:16:58.690
Isn't that one of his weapons, though?

00:17:01.950 --> 00:17:04.140
Don't look at anything you don't need to.

00:17:04.530 --> 00:17:06.040
Next will be another "E."

00:17:06.920 --> 00:17:08.060
On the west side.

00:17:08.430 --> 00:17:10.260
On this screen, the left side.

00:17:10.260 --> 00:17:12.050
An "E" on the left side?

00:17:12.050 --> 00:17:13.510
ERIDER?

00:17:14.610 --> 00:17:17.970
We've identified the next point at which 
the unmanned motorcycle will appear,

00:17:17.970 --> 00:17:20.180
using its transit route thus far.

00:17:17.970 --> 00:17:20.180
<b>Conference Room 1 

00:17:20.180 --> 00:17:22.550
We believe the criminal is doing this for fun.

00:17:22.550 --> 00:17:25.600
We'll make a cordon around "L"

00:17:25.600 --> 00:17:27.100
and deploy our personnel there.

00:17:27.100 --> 00:17:27.810
Yes, sir!

00:17:29.650 --> 00:17:31.750
This is Team A. We're in position.

00:17:31.750 --> 00:17:34.460
Teams B and C will arrive soon.

00:17:33.330 --> 00:17:36.580
Mobile Traffic is staking out point "L," after all.

00:17:36.580 --> 00:17:39.990
We'll go to the "E" on the opposite side.

00:17:39.990 --> 00:17:42.650
No harm in staking out both, right?

00:17:42.650 --> 00:17:45.280
And we're betting on him.

00:17:45.280 --> 00:17:48.710
Not taking advantage of his 
talent would be a waste.

00:17:48.960 --> 00:17:52.630
But he's being held as someone 
dangerous, isn't he?

00:17:52.630 --> 00:17:55.820
His life was warped.

00:17:55.820 --> 00:17:58.010
If it can be straightened out,

00:17:58.360 --> 00:17:59.780
I'd like to try.

00:18:00.140 --> 00:18:02.560
<b>Target</b>

00:18:00.950 --> 00:18:02.560
Target motorcycle has appeared.

00:18:02.560 --> 00:18:03.730
Okay, where?

00:18:03.730 --> 00:18:05.310
Going in the other direction.

00:18:05.310 --> 00:18:06.020
What?

00:18:06.370 --> 00:18:07.690
We're on our way!

00:18:07.690 --> 00:18:09.250
Keep pursuing it!

00:18:09.600 --> 00:18:12.440
Whoever is remote controlling 
this, can you hear me?

00:18:12.440 --> 00:18:15.010
Move your Willwear to the side 
of the road, and power down!

00:18:15.010 --> 00:18:16.910
Repeat, move your Willwear—

00:18:18.410 --> 00:18:19.780
You know...

00:18:20.180 --> 00:18:23.370
I know exactly where you're going!

00:18:23.370 --> 00:18:25.370
They came here after all.

00:18:25.370 --> 00:18:27.270
Kyoukai-san, this Willwear...

00:18:27.270 --> 00:18:28.390
I've got it here.

00:18:28.390 --> 00:18:30.130
No life signs, just like we thought.

00:18:30.130 --> 00:18:32.040
No need to hold back, then!

00:18:33.550 --> 00:18:34.720
It accelerated!

00:18:34.720 --> 00:18:35.910
Oscar III!

00:18:35.910 --> 00:18:37.610
Congratulations, Kyoukai-san!

00:18:37.610 --> 00:18:38.800
We get to test this...

00:18:39.450 --> 00:18:41.140
Mjölnir Mode II!

00:18:43.890 --> 00:18:44.640
Huh?

00:18:46.940 --> 00:18:48.810
What the heck?!

00:18:49.060 --> 00:18:50.870
The movements are following a program.

00:18:50.870 --> 00:18:52.680
He was right...

00:18:53.350 --> 00:18:54.780
Next will be another "E."

00:18:55.090 --> 00:18:56.190
On the west side.

00:18:56.190 --> 00:18:58.090
On this screen, the left side.

00:18:58.090 --> 00:18:59.920
An "E"? ERIDER?

00:18:59.920 --> 00:19:02.610
He's deliberately using one-way 
streets the wrong way.

00:19:02.610 --> 00:19:05.120
In other words, that's how 
he wants us to read it.

00:19:05.360 --> 00:19:07.130
REDIRE?

00:19:07.130 --> 00:19:08.080
What's that?

00:19:08.880 --> 00:19:09.830
Latin.

00:19:10.820 --> 00:19:11.990
Latin?

00:19:11.990 --> 00:19:13.260
Indeed.

00:19:13.790 --> 00:19:16.130
"Redire." It means

00:19:16.820 --> 00:19:18.130
"to return."

00:19:18.130 --> 00:19:20.100
Return? What's returning?

00:19:20.400 --> 00:19:21.440
Bird.

00:19:22.760 --> 00:19:24.900
That's one hell of an elaborate trick to play!

00:19:24.900 --> 00:19:28.770
No, he never did anything without reason.

00:19:28.770 --> 00:19:30.920
Yeah, he's not playing around.

00:19:30.920 --> 00:19:33.270
Most likely, there's another aspect.

00:19:33.270 --> 00:19:34.360
But...

00:19:35.700 --> 00:19:39.460
The Willwear probably has a 
monitoring transmitter on it.

00:19:39.740 --> 00:19:42.240
There's something I want you to do with it.

00:19:43.320 --> 00:19:45.910
I guess I'll grant his wish.

00:19:47.020 --> 00:19:49.620
Striking Crusher Cannon,

00:19:50.620 --> 00:19:51.290
fire!

00:19:56.420 --> 00:19:57.610
I see...

00:19:57.610 --> 00:19:59.720
So the present was successfully received.

00:20:00.930 --> 00:20:02.510
It was simple.

00:20:02.940 --> 00:20:05.260
I sent the traffic cops running around the city,

00:20:05.480 --> 00:20:07.700
and then directed it through the gaps.

00:20:09.090 --> 00:20:11.480
Okay, I'm looking forward to seeing you.

00:20:12.370 --> 00:20:15.020
So it got caught, huh?

00:20:15.020 --> 00:20:17.150
Then I'll turn off the system...

00:20:22.420 --> 00:20:23.510
Mythos?

00:20:31.750 --> 00:20:33.540
I'm back.

00:20:33.540 --> 00:20:35.260
W-Welcome back.

00:20:35.260 --> 00:20:36.860
Um...

00:20:36.860 --> 00:20:37.800
We're sorry!

00:20:37.800 --> 00:20:39.980
Don't tell me you're sorry!

00:20:39.980 --> 00:20:43.260
What am I supposed to do with 
this stack of bar receipts?!

00:20:43.260 --> 00:20:44.700
Jeez...

00:20:47.680 --> 00:20:49.020
What is this?!

00:20:49.020 --> 00:20:50.780
That was Kuroki-san.

00:20:50.780 --> 00:20:52.890
I thought it was wrong, too, but...

00:20:52.890 --> 00:20:57.470
Sena-kun, even if there's an extra charge 
for cleaning private spaces...

00:20:57.470 --> 00:20:59.410
No, it was bothering me,

00:20:59.410 --> 00:21:00.910
so I did clean it,

00:21:00.910 --> 00:21:03.350
but he got worse every day.

00:21:04.860 --> 00:21:07.590
And his territory expanded every day...

00:21:07.590 --> 00:21:08.550
Where is he?

00:21:08.550 --> 00:21:10.330
Where did Kuroki-kun go?

00:21:10.590 --> 00:21:12.130
He's dealing with that other matter.

00:21:12.130 --> 00:21:13.290
That other matter?

00:21:13.290 --> 00:21:16.410
Oh, the one Hayashida-san reported on?

00:21:19.120 --> 00:21:19.810
Hey.

00:21:21.240 --> 00:21:22.590
Want to go outside?

00:21:26.120 --> 00:21:27.860
If he's coming back,

00:21:27.860 --> 00:21:30.100
we want someone who can fight him.

00:21:30.390 --> 00:21:32.720
And that someone is me?

00:21:32.720 --> 00:21:34.880
You want to get back at him, right?

00:21:35.990 --> 00:21:37.720
I got permission from above.

00:21:37.720 --> 00:21:40.610
For cooperating with the investigation,
you can have a degree of freedom.

00:21:41.250 --> 00:21:43.570
But you've gotta keep this GPS bracelet on.

00:21:43.570 --> 00:21:45.830
You'll be the one observing me?

00:21:45.830 --> 00:21:46.620
Yeah.

00:21:46.620 --> 00:21:49.530
You deleted your own data from 
the government systems, right?

00:21:49.530 --> 00:21:51.940
You need to be registered to some country,

00:21:51.940 --> 00:21:55.320
so the documents say that 
you're my little brother.

00:21:56.330 --> 00:21:58.470
You have three choices!

00:21:59.040 --> 00:22:00.750
One, Kuroki Jirou.

00:22:01.150 --> 00:22:03.350
Two, Kuroki Shimajirou.

00:22:03.350 --> 00:22:05.670
Three, Kuroki Nobujirou.

00:22:06.600 --> 00:22:08.400
So I'm stuck with "Jirou"?

00:22:08.720 --> 00:22:10.670
You're my little brother, after all.

00:22:11.680 --> 00:22:13.570
Nice to meet you, Jirou!

00:22:13.870 --> 00:22:17.780
Can I at least have the right 
to choose my own name?

00:23:50.110 --> 00:23:52.110
<b>Next Episode Preview</b>

00:23:51.030 --> 00:23:52.270
I'm not saying it.

00:23:52.270 --> 00:23:54.980
Huh, then maybe I will...

00:23:52.450 --> 00:24:04.990
File 5: Who Benefits?

00:23:54.980 --> 00:23:57.510
Bird, if you're saying it otherwise, I will.

00:23:58.970 --> 00:24:00.190
Ohakonyapachininko.

00:24:01.090 --> 00:24:03.550
You fell for it, Jirou-kun.

00:24:03.550 --> 00:24:04.860
Don't call me that!
